<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korean bond market closed on holidays.</title>
<headline>South Korean bond market closed on holidays.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's bond market is closed on Friday and Saturday for Lunar New Year holidays. The market will reopen next Monday.</p>
<p>Yields on benchmark three-year corporate bonds closed flat at 12.00 percent on Thursday. Three-month CD yields also closed unchanged at 12.25 percent.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
